Titre$The genus Phellodon by Gordon Dickson
com$tiré de British fungi Keys / adapt GF 09/2014



1,2 $ Stipe black, pileus some shade of 'black'
1,3 $ Stipe and pileus some shade of brown
2,0 $ Cap zoned with a white edge, centre commencing brown and becoming brown-black; pileoli usually fused, not overlapping; with pine, spruce or birch$melaleucus
2,0 $ Cap with sharply defined white edge, centre with blue-black silky tomentum without shades of brown; pileoli usually overlapping; with oak in the south, pine or spruce in the north $ niger
3,0 $ Multiple, zoned pileoli, usually fused; with pine or spruce $ tomentosum
3,0 $  Cap buff coloured, greying with age, not or only slightly zoned, stipe tomentose; with broad-leaf trees confluens$confluens
